---
import ProgrammerCatImage from "../assets/programmer-cat.jpg";
import Layout from "../layouts/BlogPost.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Services"
  description="Sylvia's software services"
  pubDate={new Date("October 14 2026")}
  heroImage={ProgrammerCatImage}
>
  <h2>Contact Info</h2>

  <p>
    Contact me on <a
      href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sylviamirecki/"
      target="_blank">LinkedIn</a
    > with your needs and we can set up a meeting.
  </p>

  <h2>High performance computing</h2>

  <p>
    I'm looking for teams who need to scale their data infrastructure, optimize
    distributed systems, or build high-throughput pipelines. If you want to cut
    costs, boost speed, or reduce the number of compute nodes you require, hit
    me up!
  </p>

  <h4>Why me?</h4>
  <div class="hpc-highlight">
    <ul>
      <li>
        Redesigned caching mechanism with Redis to reduce costs 5x-20x and
        designed distributed data apps with Scala, Spark, and Python at Amazon
        Alexa.
      </li>
      <li>
        Redesigned ETL pipeline to cut back 3p onboarding time from weeks to
        days via Scala code generation at Amazon Alexa.
      </li>
      <li>
        Wrote a B compiler in Rust with a highly parallel compiler pipeline
        running at 3 million LOC/second, featuring a recursive descent parser
        with SIMD lexing, an embedded linker, an optimizer, and a single
        dependency jemalloc.
      </li>
      <li>
        Solved distributed system failures through metrics and massive log
        stores across Go and Rust services at Dropbox.
      </li>
      <li>
        Improved drivers, bootloaders, and system functions for
        indoor-positioning systems and flying machines using ARM C and C++ at
        Verity Studios AG.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h4>What am I offering?</h4>
  <p>
    I'll build you reliable high performance software to fix any bottlenecks you
    have in your system.
  </p>

  <h2>Multimedia processing components</h2>
  
  <p>
    I'm looking for teams or creators who need custom video/audio processing,
    real-time pipelines, or custom GStreamer plugins. If you want to push the
    boundaries of multimedia, I would be giddy to build for you!
  </p>

  <h4>Why me?</h4>
  <div class="media-highlight">
    <ul>
      <li>
        Implemented a real-time multimedia (video/audio) processing pipeline in
        Rust with a hand-rolled stream-based recursive descent parser at
        Searchless.
      </li>
      <li>
        Built custom GStreamer components for video postprocessing at
        Searchless.
      </li>
      <li>
        Developed Wavy Crockett, a software audio synthesizer platform in Rust
        featuring a custom Lisp interpreter, fundamental audio building blocks
        (sine waves, square waves, white noise, ADSR envelopes, gaussian blurs),
        LFO envelopes, drum synthesis, chord progressions, and sequencing.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h4>What am I offering?</h4>
  <p>
    I'll build you the tools you need, whether it's real-time video pipelines,
    A/V effect plugins, or multimedia integrations with any stack.
  </p>

  <h2>Audio synthesizers</h2>

  <p>
    I'm looking for musicians who are looking to tune into the "oldschool
    computer" sounds. If you want an easy way to interact with an old audio chip
    like the POKEY or C64 SID, I'm your girl 😎
  </p>

  <div class="pokey-video">
    <video controls>
      <source src="/video/pokey_mario_lowres.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      Your browser does not support the video tag.
    </video>
  </div>

  <h4>Why me?</h4>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Hand-wired a 6502 computer (Phlogiston 6502) following the Eater 6502 kit,
      extracted a POKEY chip from a broken Atari 800 from the scrapyard, and
      rewired the computer to incorporate POKEY audio synthesis and I/O muxing.
    </li>
    <li>
      Developed Wavy Crockett, a software audio synthesizer platform in Rust
      featuring a custom Lisp interpreter, fundamental audio building blocks
      (sine waves, square waves, white noise, ADSR envelopes, gaussian blurs),
      LFO envelopes, drum synthesis, chord progressions, and sequencing.
    </li>
    <li>
      I have a degree in Physics and have done quite a lot of hobby electronics
      work (as shown in the video above), plus an internship in Embedded
      Software Engineering.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h4>What am I offering?</h4>

  <p>
    I'll build you custom hardware for easily interfacing with old audio chips
    however you like - be that knobs and dials or MIDI. I'm also open to
    touring, but I'm definitely not a composer so you would have to boss me
    around and tell me what bleeps and bloops to make.
  </p>
</Layout>

<style>
  .pokey-video {
    margin-top: 1em;
    margin-bottom: 2em;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .pokey-video video {
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
</style>
